### Describe the bug

#66912 reports the same root cause for `[FromBody(EmptyBodyBehavior = Allow)]`. #67591 fixed it for 11.0; this asks for that fix in 10.0 servicing.

With `EnableRequestDelegateGenerator` (on by default under `PublishAot` and `PublishTrimmed`), the generator in 10.0 gives one interceptor to minimal API handlers with the same HTTP method and return type whose parameters have the same types and names, even when their binding attributes differ. The second endpoint then binds its parameters as the first one does:

- `MapGet("/query", (Guid id) => ...)` and `MapGet("/header", ([FromHeader(Name = "X-Id")] Guid id) => ...)`: `/header` reads `id` from the route or the query string. A request carrying the `X-Id` header gets 400, and `/header?id=...` without the header gets 200.
- `([FromHeader(Name = "X-A")] string value)` and `([FromHeader(Name = "X-B")] string value)`: `/header-b` reads the `X-A` header.

The build reports no warning or diagnostic, and startup no error. With the generator off, every endpoint binds as written.

On `release/10.0` (55d77e1), endpoints are grouped with `Endpoint.SignatureEquals` ([Endpoint.cs#L116-L134](https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/blob/55d77e1e0349aa2a079a516f6ecb7c79b56bf85c/src/Http/Http.Extensions/gen/Microsoft.AspNetCore.Http.RequestDelegateGenerator/StaticRouteHandlerModel/Endpoint.cs#L116-L134)), which compares parameters with `EndpointParameter.SignatureEquals`: type, symbol name and keyed-service key only ([EndpointParameter.cs#L604-L611](https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/blob/55d77e1e0349aa2a079a516f6ecb7c79b56bf85c/src/Http/Http.Extensions/gen/Microsoft.AspNetCore.Http.RequestDelegateGenerator/StaticRouteHandlerModel/EndpointParameter.cs#L604-L611)). #67591 replaced it on `main` with `EndpointParameter.Equals`, which also compares the binding source, the lookup name, the ordinal and optionality, and added `MapAction_ExplicitHeaderParam_SharedDelegateSignature_PreservesBindingName`, which covers the header-name case above. On 11.0.0-rc.1 every endpoint of the repro binds correctly.

For the servicing decision:

- Impact: in an app that enables the generator (every app published with `PublishAot` or `PublishTrimmed`) and has two such handlers, the second binds from another source or under another name, with no diagnostic. 10.0 is an LTS release.
- Regression: no. `release/8.0` and `release/9.0` have the same comparison.
- Risk: low. The change (8 lines added and 11 removed in two files, whose context matches `release/10.0`) and its regression tests have been on `main` since 11.0-preview7 and ship in 11.0 RC1.
- Workaround: give the parameters of such handlers different names.

### Expected Behavior

Each endpoint binds its parameters as its own attributes say, with the generator on or off, as on 11.0.0-rc.1.

### Steps To Reproduce

Repro project: https://github.com/AdCodicem/dotnet-upstream-repros/tree/main/aspnetcore-rdg-shared-interceptor. `./repro.sh` builds and runs it with the generator off, then on; `REPRO_TFM=net11.0 ./repro.sh` does the same on .NET 11.

`Repro.csproj` (the repository's version takes the target framework from `REPRO_TFM`; `net10.0` is its default):

```xml
<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Web">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <EnableRequestDelegateGenerator>true</EnableRequestDelegateGenerator>
    <EmitCompilerGeneratedFiles>true</EmitCompilerGeneratedFiles>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
```

`Program.cs`:

```csharp
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc;

var builder = WebApplication.CreateSlimBuilder(args);
builder.Logging.ClearProviders();
builder.WebHost.UseUrls("http://127.0.0.1:0");
var app = builder.Build();

// Same parameter type and name; only the binding attributes differ.
app.MapGet("/query", (Guid id) => $"query {id}");
app.MapGet("/header", ([FromHeader(Name = "X-Id")] Guid id) => $"header {id}");

// Same source, different header names.
app.MapGet("/header-a", ([FromHeader(Name = "X-A")] string value) => $"X-A {value}");
app.MapGet("/header-b", ([FromHeader(Name = "X-B")] string value) => $"X-B {value}");

await app.StartAsync();
using var client = new HttpClient { BaseAddress = new Uri(app.Urls.First()) };

var id = Guid.NewGuid();
await Send("/query?id=" + id, null);
await Send("/header", ("X-Id", id.ToString()));
await Send("/header-a", ("X-A", "a"));
await Send("/header-b", ("X-B", "b"));

// What the second endpoint of each pair actually binds.
await Send("/header?id=" + id, null);
await Send("/header-b", ("X-A", "a"));

await app.StopAsync();

async Task Send(string path, (string Name, string Value)? header)
{
    using var request = new HttpRequestMessage(HttpMethod.Get, path);
    if (header is { } h) request.Headers.Add(h.Name, h.Value);
    using var response = await client.SendAsync(request);
    var body = await response.Content.ReadAsStringAsync();
    Console.WriteLine($"GET {path,-48} {(header is { } x ? x.Name + ": " + x.Value : ""),-44} -> {(int)response.StatusCode} {body}");
}
```

